   <p>To his Ecxcellency the <persName ref="cwgk:N001000">Governor</persName> of the <orgName ref="cwgk:O001025">Commonwealth of Kentucky</orgName>,</p>
<p>The undersigned Citizens of <placeName ref="cwgk:P00000544">Pendleton County</placeName> and neighbors of <persName ref="cwgk:N00014113">Wm H Gardner</persName> State that the <hi rend="str">Sad</hi> Said Gardner was fined under an indictment in the <orgName ref="cwgk:O00000489">Pendleton Circuit Court</orgName> in the Sum of three hundred dollars $300 -- 00 and costs at <hi rend="str">its</hi> the <date when="1865-10">Oct Term 1865</date>. of Said court under the charge of Keeping a gambling house in Said County Some five years ago. The gambling took place in the bar room over which <persName ref="cwgk:N00014110">a man by the name of Brown</persName> had the exclusive control, and over which Said Gardner assumed no control, Said Gardner is a poor man, and we recommend him under the Circumstances to your Clemency, <date when="1865-12-12">Decr 12<hi rend="sup">th</hi> 1865</date>,</p>
<p><milestone unit="column" n="2"/><cb n="1"/><persName ref="cwgk:N00003852">Jas. I. Hudnall</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00003781">W<hi rend="sup">m</hi> Childes</persName>
<lb/><hi rend="underline">M</hi> <hi rend="underline">Mullins</hi>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00003853">Geo W Jameson</persName>
<lb/><persName ref="cwgk:N00014111">Josiah M<hi rend="sup">c</hi>Kinly</persName>
